{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-25T05:50:53.377Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1780"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1780: the runRegisteredCommandForTest doc says undeclared option keys pass through, but the harness refuses them with unknown_option on a command that declares flags"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH-1780 (filed 2026-11-24 by the package-fleet maintainer after the 2026.11.14 to 2026.11.2x migration). The JSDoc of runRegisteredCommandForTest (bound as harness.runCommand) in src/sdk/testing.ts, published in dist/sdk/testing.d.ts, ends its option contract with 'and undeclared keys pass through'. Since the host alignment of pm-gh1726/pm-gh1727 the direct-caller normalizer (normalizeDirectExtensionCommandOptions) refuses a key that is neither a declared spelling nor a host-owned option with unknown_option (exit 2) before dispatch, on every extension-created command path that declares flags. Undeclared keys still pass through in three cases only: a command that declares no flags (pm-4of199 owns that refusal), a hand-built registry with no flag registrations, and a native core command path an extension extends or overrides. An array for a scalar flag is refused with extension_flag_value_invalid. Reproduced on 2026.11.25 by reading the normalizer: refuseUnknownExtensionOption runs for every non-host key when declaredDefinitions is non-empty and the policy is refuse. docs/SDK.md repeats the sentence for the harness but correctly scopes hand-built registries. Fleet impact (from the report): the largest single failure class of the migration, about 25 suites across pm-slack-standup, pm-todos, pm-github, pm-brief, pm-context and pm-screen; the refusal read like a harness bug. Duplicate check: searched runCommand undeclared option pass through unknown_option harness; pm-gh1665 (closed) shipped the normalizer, pm-4of199 (open) owns zero-flag refusal, pm-gh1731 and pm-gh1657 own migration notes and SDK release-note lines."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","docs","extensions","gh:1780","sdk","testing"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-25T05:50:53.377Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-25T05:50:53.377Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":60},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The runRegisteredCommandForTest JSDoc and the docs/SDK.md harness paragraph state the current rule: undeclared keys are refused with unknown_option before dispatch on a command that declares flags, exactly as the CLI refuses an unknown flag, and an array for a scalar flag is refused with extension_flag_value_invalid; Both texts name the three cases that still pass undeclared keys through (zero-flag command, hand-built registry, native core path) and the supported way to unit-test a handler with a free option bag; A harness test pins each documented case so the text cannot drift from behaviour again"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-ugqx"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reporter","value":"unbraind"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Package authors reading the harness contract learn that undeclared keys are refused on declared-flag commands, and which cases pass them through"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-4of199","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-25T05:50:53.377Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1657","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-25T05:50:53.377Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1665","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-25T05:50:53.377Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1726","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-25T05:50:53.377Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1727","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-25T05:50:53.377Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1731","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-25T05:50:53.377Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"9b44fcb5f088263c83fa7950ed4e9fbdc03e972e3d7ffdba5c05b796740b1fa6","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f6ea77604b47fc38111a52dbb4fbf3811b107a8b767c2cfc83e0d6d283d7dd6f"}
